WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is a very funny

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
Emmy-winning
writer and comedian.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
She executive produced
the docuseries,

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.272 line:92%
"Visible: Out on Television,

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is streaming
on Apple TV+.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's my conversation
with Wanda Sykes.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wanda, it's so good
to see you again.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.315 line:92%
-Oh, good to see you too, Seth

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:18.418
-We're obviously living throug
some difficult times right now

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
but are you drawing any help
from the protest movement

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we've seen
in this last month?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I am. I am.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they look
a lot different now.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
They are very diverse.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:36.469
We have a lot of young peopl
out there, which is great.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it feels different.
It really does.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're --
it keeps going, you know?

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it gets bigger,
it's growing.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I am --
I'm hopeful.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:52.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When this first started,
hopefully, I heard this right,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
that your instinct
was not to go to march,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.624
but then you were sort of
overcome by this movement,

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.361 size:84% position:42%
and you and your wife
and your kids went out?

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah, it was that night

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I had some --
I had a few tequilas,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, and it was just
one thing after the other.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, I just --
I just lost it.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just had to talk
to some people

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:27.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
and went on Instagram
and went live.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.688 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, um...

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.823 line:92%
Yeah, and I meant what I said.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.125
I was like, you know, I'm not --
I'm not doing it.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:35.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not our problem.
We keep doing the same thing

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
We keep marching,
and nothing changes.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, we're the victim
of the problem.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's your problem.
You have to fix your problem

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I, you know,
saw the marches

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:53.880
and how many people are ou
and the response and all

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
from, you know -- from
the George Floyd execution

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.988 line:92%
it gave me hope, you know?

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.224 line:92%
Especially when I saw, also,

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
religious leaders
speaking out, too.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was like, "Okay. Now folk
are getting it," you know?

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
It felt like people
were getting it.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:19.172 size:88% position:44%
-How did your children
like being at the march?

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they loved
the marching part.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:25.845
But then, once the stationar
part happened, and, you know

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're listening
to all the speakers,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.383 line:92%
then they were bored silly

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-They were --

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just wanted to go home.
They were hot.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.923
And I think -- I'm pretty sure
my daughter faked a heat stroke.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm pretty sure.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just like,
"Ah! Ah! Ah!"

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Okay.
That's good.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a good one.
That's good," so...

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
In your fantastic last special
"Not Normal,"

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.839 size:88% position:44%
you talk about the fact
that your wife is white,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:53.673 size:88% position:44% line:92%
your children are white.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
How has it been in this moment
talking to them?

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.979
Because I would imagine
children have a curiosity

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.981 line:92%
as to why people are so upset.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man.
You know -- [ Chuckles ]

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:11.391
It's been difficult, because
you know, I have to tune it out.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.392 line:92%
I have to turn it off sometimes,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:17.664
because there's always something
that will just make me go nuts

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just -- I just --
I just get so angry and hurt

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:29.442
And, actually, I talked to som
of my black friends about it

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.343 line:92%
especially my sorority sisters

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:33.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
They, all their kids are older
and everything now,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.781 line:92%
so they've been through it

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I'm like,
"Look, I'm having issues.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:42.121
I'm trying to talk to my son
about the George Floyd case,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.356 line:92%
and he's like, 'Uh-huh.'"

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"So, the police officer,

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.727 line:92%
he had his knee on his neck.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my son's like,
"Yeah, that's bad.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
He killed him."
I said, "Yeah."

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes,
"He should go to jail."

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Yeah, Lucas, you get it."

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.004
And he goes, "Um, so what'
your favorite dinosaur?"

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "What? What?"
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:05.311
You know, that's kids --
"I got it. Let's move on.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
Next topic," you know?
So...

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:08.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I have to just let the
be kids, you know?

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.455 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's like, you can't --

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what
my friends were saying.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "Look, let them
enjoy their innocence,

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
and let them be kids.
You're raising good kids.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.298 size:81% position:41% line:92%
They'll get it," so...

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:28.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want my kids
to later in life, you know

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:31.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone ask them,
"So, what was your mom like?

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.173
and they're like, "Whoa,
that was one angry bitch.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me tell you."
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Ooh, she was mad.
Hoo!"

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, my next question
was gonna be

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.616 line:92%
what your favorite dinosaur is

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
but now I feel like
I should skip it.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:50.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wait. If Lucas ever finds out,
tell him to text me.

